{"blocks":[["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/07%20Divide/Asset/01-Divide-screen/png/","source-block-43","01 Divide screen",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-229","Trimming project beginnings and ends",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-270","Cut unwanted material from the start and end of a recording. Set the starting and ending points of the part to keep.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-390","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select PROJECT (MULTI FILE mode) or FILE LIST (STEREO FILE mode).",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-512","2. Select the project or file to trim, then select EDIT > TRIM.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-581","3. Use the scroll button to select the starting point icon.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-644","Trim screen",["Trimming project beginnings and ends","3. Use the scroll button to select the starting point icon."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-826","The line under the bar shows the starting time and ending time of the part to keep.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends","3. Use the scroll button to select the starting point icon."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-914","4. Use Back and Forward to find the starting point.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-1055","5. Use the scroll button to select the ending point icon, then set the ending point the same way.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-1156","6. Press REC.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/","source-block-1177","7. Select YES.",["Trimming project beginnings and ends"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/08%20Trim/Asset/01-Trim-screen/png/","source-block-43","01 Trim screen",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-230","Deleting multiple files",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-258","Delete files that are no longer needed.",["Deleting multiple files"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-301","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select PROJECT (MULTI FILE mode) or FILE LIST (STEREO FILE mode).",["Deleting multiple files"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-423","2. Open the list of files to delete.",["Deleting multiple files"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-463","MULTI FILE mode: select a project, then select FILE DELETE.",["Deleting multiple files","2. Open the list of files to delete."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-529","STEREO FILE mode: press REC.",["Deleting multiple files","2. Open the list of files to delete."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-566","3. Select each file to delete. A checked box marks each selected file.",["Deleting multiple files"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-640","File delete list",["Deleting multiple files","3. Select each file to delete. A checked box marks each selected file."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-845","Press PLAY/PAUSE to select or clear all files.",["Deleting multiple files","3. Select each file to delete. A checked box marks each selected file."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-900","Press MENU to cancel file deletion.",["Deleting multiple files","3. Select each file to delete. A checked box marks each selected file."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-944","4. Press REC.",["Deleting multiple files"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/","source-block-965","5. Select YES.",["Deleting multiple files"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/09%20Delete%20Files/Asset/01-File-delete-list/png/","source-block-43","01 File delete list",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-238","Deleting multiple projects",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-269","MULTI FILE mode only. Delete several projects in the selected folder at once. The folder is chosen in Zoom H5/UG/08 Recording/07 Save Location.",["Deleting multiple projects"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-420","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select PROJECT.",["Deleting multiple projects"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-490","2. Press REC.",["Deleting multiple projects"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-511","3. Select each project to delete. A checked box marks each selected project.",["Deleting multiple projects"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-591","Project delete list",["Deleting multiple projects","3. Select each project to delete. A checked box marks each selected project."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-808","Press PLAY/PAUSE to select or clear all projects.",["Deleting multiple projects","3. Select each project to delete. A checked box marks each selected project."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-866","Press MENU to cancel project deletion.",["Deleting multiple projects","3. Select each project to delete. A checked box marks each selected project."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-913","4. Press REC.",["Deleting multiple projects"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/","source-block-934","5. Select YES.",["Deleting multiple projects"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/10%20Delete%20Projects/Asset/01-Project-delete-list/png/","source-block-43","01 Project delete list",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/11%20Rebuild%20Project/","source-block-237","Rebuilding a project",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/11%20Rebuild%20Project/","source-block-262","MULTI FILE mode only. Rebuild a project that is damaged or missing files it needs.",["Rebuilding a project"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/11%20Rebuild%20Project/","source-block-348","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select PROJECT.",["Rebuilding a project"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/11%20Rebuild%20Project/","source-block-418","2. Select the project to rebuild, then select REBUILD.",["Rebuilding a project"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/11%20Rebuild%20Project/","source-block-478","3. Select YES.",["Rebuilding a project"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-172","Adding voice memos",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-195","MULTI FILE mode only. Record a spoken memo and attach it to a project.",["Adding voice memos"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-269","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select PROJECT.",["Adding voice memos"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-339","2. Select the project for the memo, then select OPTION > VOICE MEMO.",["Adding voice memos"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-413","3. Record the memo.",["Adding voice memos"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-436","Voice memo screen",["Adding voice memos","3. Record the memo."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-643","Press REC to start recording.",["Adding voice memos","3. Record the memo."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-681","Press STOP or REC to stop recording.",["Adding voice memos","3. Record the memo."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-730","4. Play the memo.",["Adding voice memos"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-751","Press PLAY/PAUSE to start playback.",["Adding voice memos","4. Play the memo."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/","source-block-795","Press STOP to stop playback.",["Adding voice memos","4. Play the memo."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/10%20Project%20and%20File%20Editing/12%20Voice%20Memos/Asset/01-Voice-memo-screen/png/","source-block-43","01 Voice memo screen",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/","source-block-156","USB functions",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-130","Data exchange with computers (card reader)",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-177","Connected to a computer, the H5 works as a card reader, so you can check and copy the data on its SD card.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-287","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select USB > SD CARD READER.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-370","2. Connect the H5's USB port to the computer with a USB cable.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-440","Connecting to a computer",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)","2. Connect the H5's USB port to the computer with a USB cable."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-774","3. Before unplugging the cable, disconnect the H5 on the computer.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-844","Windows: use Safely Remove Hardware and select the H5.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)","3. Before unplugging the cable, disconnect the H5 on the computer."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-907","Mac: drag the H5 icon to the Trash.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)","3. Before unplugging the cable, disconnect the H5 on the computer."]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/","source-block-1018","4. Unplug the cable from the computer and the H5, then press MENU.",["Data exchange with computers (card reader)"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/01%20Card%20Reader/Asset/01-Connecting-to-a-computer/png/","source-block-43","01 Connecting to a computer",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/02%20Audio%20Interface/","source-block-177","Using as an audio interface",[]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/02%20Audio%20Interface/","source-block-209","Over USB, the H5 sends the signals at its inputs straight to a computer or iPad, and plays that device's audio back out through the H5.",["Using as an audio interface"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/02%20Audio%20Interface/","source-block-348","1. Press MENU, then use the scroll button to select USB > AUDIO INTERFACE.",["Using as an audio interface"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/02%20Audio%20Interface/","source-block-432","2. Select STEREO or MULTI TRACK, and press the scroll button.",["Using as an audio interface"]],["Zoom%20H5/UG/11%20USB/02%20Audio%20Interface/","source-block-501","STEREO — a 2-in/2-out interface for a computer or an iPad. It needs no driver. USB 2.0 Full Speed, 44.1/48 kHz, 16-bit.",["Using as an audio interface","2. Select STEREO or MULTI TRACK, and press the scroll button."]]],"format_version":5}